rix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the missing elementary column operations?" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162561 1072 #uuid "44844b50-2f6e-5293-a5b6-be91cc0464d5" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162562 1068 #edb/ref 17592186160634 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162562 1069 "q-42917" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162562 1071 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_{i}:=C_{i} + kC_{3}$, the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the elementary column operations?" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162562 1072 #uuid "a68c2e7c-c605-5187-a1fa-13349acf01b6" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162563 1068 #edb/ref 17592186160640 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162563 1069 "q-59965" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162563 1071 "![](images/7f/7fd9ec533805c0d583ec0e6c28954a74e3e23d2928252243ede810f86af50bea.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162563 1072 #uuid "f3ab8fe9-b22b-5ca6-bd8b-10d532cbb162" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162564 1068 #edb/ref 17592186160646 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162564 1069 "q-59966" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162564 1071 "![](images/b2/b21e3616f863aa4f1593918e451d3d05e1a3bfed9e99f36d34814d1ddeaff520.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162564 1072 #uuid "5230515f-54bb-5369-8290-c13d16ba0e2a" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162565 1068 #edb/ref 17592186160652 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162565 1069 "q-60310" 13194139533366 17592186045585 true] [17592186162565 1071 "![](images/9a/9a3561a1c31d744f5